/T (ABSTRACT)
/E (ABSTRACT)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
78 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (Environmental pollution poses significant sustainability challenges to human health, the environment, and natural resources. Cases of air pollution, water pollution, waste disposal, soil pollution, and noise pollution are common in residential and urban areas. However, most of these occurrences are only visible to the human eye but rarely are reported or monitored by the appropriate authorities and local inhabitants. Current complaint systems only deal with complaints and do not offer any form of immediate location-based alerts or updates to the affected systems.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
79 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (Therefore, this paper proposes a Smart Pollution Alert and Location-Based Environmental Notification System. The idea is to come up with an IT system that offers immediate information dissemination on environmental pollution incidents reported. The proposed system will have various features, including collecting the required information about the incident, classifying the type and severity of the pollution cases, and offering relevant information to the affected locations. Additionally, the system will be able to store the details retrieved about the pollution event in a database and used to generate statistics and reports.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (It is envisioned that the pollution alert system will be developed as a responsive website that can be accessed through desktop and mobile devices. It will also be possible to monitor and include all the relevant information about the pollution incident detected. The system will open new dimensions in environmental monitoring, management, and pollution reporting while promoting sustainable development and supporting selected SDGs and environmental management principles. Furthermore, future implementations can include the use of GIS and IoT to monitor and collect real-time data using sensors and data analytics.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
81 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 61 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
/A [223 0 R 0]
/K [4]
>>
endobj
82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 62 0 R
/T (INTRODUCTION)
/E (INTRODUCTION)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Environmental pollution is a serious threat to the ecosystem that consists of atmosphere, hydrosphere, lithosphere, and other life forms. The main causes of pollution are rapid urbanization, industrialization, traffic, construction activities, and inappropriate waste disposal.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (The pollution incidents can be of various types, such as environmental pollution caused by greenhouse gases, water pollution caused by chemical wastes, land pollution due to the accumulation of non-biodegradable materials, and noise pollution due to transportation and industrial activities. Human health and the environment are significantly affected by these incidents.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (The problem with the current complaint reporting system is that most of the people witness the pollution incidents, but they do not have an effective way to report the incidents. Most complaint reporting systems focus only on collecting complaints and not on providing the necessary information about the complaint.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Information technology can play a significant role in this scenario. A web-based application can be developed to collect, store, process, and share the required information about the pollution incidents. The web-based application can utilize location-based services to provide the relevant information to the users.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (The above-mentioned idea explains the concept of the web-based pollution reporting system, which focuses on providing a platform for sharing the pollution incident reports and relevant details. The system helps to increase the awareness among the people about the adverse effects of pollution and promotes an environment-friendly society.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
