>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (Environmental pollution cases like illegal dumping, excessive smoke, water contamination, industrial emissions, and noisy disturbances may have adverse effects on the surrounding community or environment. Despite the fact that the citizens may identify these problems, the current reporting and communication methods do not offer a direct way to inform the affected people in the vicinity promptly.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (The traditional complaint mechanism focuses on complaint registration and collection. However, registering a complaint does not directly inform the citizens of an environmental pollution case in their area. Additionally, the information may be fragmented in different complaint management systems, thus, being unavailable to the ordinary user searching for pollution incidents in a specific region.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (Since pollution incidents are diverse, the impact they create is also different depending on the pollution category and location. For example, a minor waste case may be less hazardous compared to a severe air pollution incident. Therefore, an efficient complaint management system should offer differentiated information based on pollution severity and category.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (Therefore, there is a need for an IT-based solution to collect the details of a pollution incident, classify it into a particular category, define the affected area, and notify the users in this location about the problem. The Smart Pollution Alert and Location-Based Environmental Notification is a system designed to address this issue.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
